The original resampling layers attribute StyleGAN2 and op/upfirdn2d.py:
https://github.com/NVlabs/stylegan2
No rights to separately obtained NVIDIA weights or datasets are implied.

EMA's warm-start convention follows the score-SDE implementation, which
attributes fadel/pytorch_ema and TensorFlow moving-average code:
https://github.com/fadel/pytorch_ema
https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/blob/r1.13/tensorflow/python/training/moving_averages.py

Project roles, JSON configuration and BaseModel/BaseTrainer/BaseDataLoader
organization are based on the design of victoresque/pytorch-template:
https://github.com/victoresque/pytorch-template
The generic template's LeNet, classifier trainer and configuration classes
are not copied. The image-generation infrastructure is newly implemented.

No pretrained weights, datasets, Inception weights or Python wheels are
redistributed. This is a research implementation, not a claim of reproducing
published FID or bitwise equivalence to every historical runner.

